WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.720
Film Courage: Writer Elizabeth Renzetti of
Globe and Mail wrote an article recently about

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.720
Iggy Pop.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.130
I don’t know if the two of you happen to
read it?

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.169
But she basically said that “If Iggy Pop
can’t live off of his art, then what chance

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:14.660
do we all have?”

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.970
And I’ll play the part of Elizabeth for
a second.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:22.010
So she writes “A new reality has tripped
him up and it’s the same one shafting artists

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.330
all over the world.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.740
Namely that everyone wants to listen and no
one wants to pay.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.000
So in short, the cat is out of the bag in
the new electronic age with electronic devices

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.050
which estrange people from their morals also
make it easy for people to steal music (i.e.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.149
content) then pay for it.

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:40.460
We know this is something that the two of
you have had to deal with.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.969
We want to get your thoughts on it.

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:43.370
Jamin Winans: Do you want me to start?

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.570
Kiowa Winans: You did start with a hard question.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.409
Film Courage: [Laughs] No pressure!

00:00:47.409 --> 00:00:52.390
Jamin Winans: My feeling is that we’re in
a period of transition more than anything.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.710
I don’t necessarily think that what is going
on right now is the future.

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.739
I think things are always changing.

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:06.930
And yeah, I agree that right now it’s particularly
difficult to monetize your art, especially

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:16.320
if you’re trying to do something very independent
and outside of the system.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:29.860
I guess I feel like a monetized solution is
coming and we’re slowly going to enter into

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:35.380
a period where artists really find their niche
and find out how to survive.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:40.360
I think right now a lot of people are still
thinking about the hey day of the last 20

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:48.700
years where DVDs and ancillary markets were
like a big thing and the industry as a whole

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:58.531
is still kind of clinging to the money that
they were making on that market and the same

00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:03.390
thing with the music industry, it hurts right
now because we’re going through this transition.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.670
Optimistically, I think it’s going to work
its way out.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.389
Kiowa Winans: I think it’s two things.

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:17.430
I think it’s ease of access and the whole
piracy idea or movement has happened out of

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:23.629
a reaction to ease of access and things being
really overpriced.

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:29.430
I think that when I was a teenager, I spent
all my babysitting money on CD’s that cost

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:35.030
$15.00 - $18.00 dollars and I only liked one
song on the album but you’ve just shelled

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.580
out $18.00.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.799
Same with the cost of DVD’s and Blue Rays
and people keep trying really hard to keep

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:49.200
locking up territories and making region coded
disks and ultra violet this and this digital

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.579
rights management.

00:02:50.579 --> 00:02:57.660
And the longer that Hollywood and the record
industries keep trying to push people out

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:03.650
and charge them a lot, the angrier they get
and there has got to be a happy medium at

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:09.930
some point and hopefully there will be, whether
it’s a Bit Torrent bundle with a pay gate

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:17.999
or something that eliminates the barrier of
access and also eliminates the over-priced

00:03:17.999 --> 00:03:19.129
nature of what’t happening.

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:21.589
So that is my hope.

